{
  "about": "A service offered to others (service.md Offered to others, DEC-0061), for ports: peerRefusal in src/descriptor-rules.ts runs the cases — the host's check before it routes a request from anyone but the operator to a service. The classes are the organization edition's four, least sensitive first, compared exactly as written; anything else is unknown and refused before any comparison. residency lists the codes the descriptor schema's peer.residency item pattern accepts and refuses: two upper-case letters, never a user-assigned code (AA, QM–QZ, XA–XZ, ZZ). It checks the shape only, so an unassigned code such as AB passes at the boundary; whether a code is assigned is not checked here (DEC-0061, Not decided).",
